{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git status --short && git diff --check && git diff -- cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv && sed -n '1,200p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\ndiff --git a/cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv b/cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\nindex b32af41..4cc01ed 100644\n--- a/cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+++ b/cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n@@ -110,6 +110,11 @@ module ex_stage (\n   // ── Branch resolve ────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n   logic        branch_cond;\n   logic        branch_taken;\n+  logic        operands_equal;\n+  logic        operand_signs_differ;\n+  logic        magnitude_less;\n+  logic        unsigned_branch;\n+  logic        branch_less;\n   logic [31:0] branch_target;\n   logic [31:0] jump_target;\n   /* verilator lint_off UNUSEDSIGNAL */\n@@ -117,14 +122,27 @@ module ex_stage (\n   /* verilator lint_on UNUSEDSIGNAL */\n \n   always_comb begin\n+    // Equality is shared by BEQ/BNE. For ordering, operands with matching\n+    // sign bits have the same signed and unsigned order, so compare only\n+    // their low 31-bit magnitudes. Differing sign bits determine the order\n+    // directly according to the branch's signedness.\n+    operands_equal        = (rs1 == rs2);\n+    operand_signs_differ  = rs1[31] ^ rs2[31];\n+    magnitude_less        = (rs1[30:0] < rs2[30:0]);\n+    unsigned_branch       = (in.ctrl.branch_op == BR_BLTU) ||\n+                            (in.ctrl.branch_op == BR_BGEU);\n+    branch_less           = operand_signs_differ\n+                          ? (unsigned_branch ? !rs1[31] : rs1[31])\n+                          : magnitude_less;\n+\n     case (in.ctrl.branch_op)\n-      BR_BEQ:  branch_cond = (rs1 == rs2);\n-      BR_BNE:  branch_cond = (rs1 != rs2);\n-      BR_BLT:  branch_cond = ($signed(rs1) <  $signed(rs2));\n-      BR_BGE:  branch_cond = ($signed(rs1) >= $signed(rs2));\n-      BR_BLTU: branch_cond = (rs1 <  rs2);\n-      BR_BGEU: branch_cond = (rs1 >= rs2);\n-      default: branch_cond = 1'b0;\n+      BR_BEQ:  branch_cond = operands_equal;\n+      BR_BNE:  branch_cond = !operands_equal;\n+      BR_BLT,\n+      BR_BLTU: branch_cond = branch_less;\n+      BR_BGE,\n+      BR_BGEU: branch_cond = !branch_less;\n+      default:  branch_cond = 1'b0;\n     endcase\n     branch_taken  = in.ctrl.is_branch && branch_cond;\n     branch_target = in.pc + in.imm;\n# Implementation notes\n\n## Change\n\nUpdated `rtl/ex_stage.sv` branch resolution to compute operand equality once,\nuse one unsigned 31-bit comparison of the low operand bits, and select the\nsigned or unsigned ordering from the sign bits when they differ. BEQ/BNE use\nthe shared equality result; BGE/BGEU invert the corresponding less-than result.\nPipeline timing and branch target handling are unchanged.\n\n## Deviations and concerns\n\nThere were no design deviations. The timing run reports 46.799 MHz at placement\noption 0, with the worst path still crossing the register file, ID, EX, IF,\nhazard logic, and ID capture (26.662 ns). The shared comparator therefore did\nnot remove the reported top-level feedback path; a controlled before/after\ntiming comparison would be needed to attribute any Fmax change to this edit.\n\n## Checks\n\n- Verilator lint: pass, no warnings.\n- Formal: pass, 53 checks and 0 failures using the auto-selected nret=1\n  wrapper and checks.\n- Cosim: pass, both ELF checks, with `NRET=1` to match `cores/bench/core.yaml`.\n  The initial default `make cosim TARGET=bench` build used NRET=2 and failed\n  because the single-channel core has no channel-1 ports; rerunning with\n  `NRET=1` built and passed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
