{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"agent_message","text":"The timing report still showed the dmem path passing through the general ALU’s result mux and multiplier logic. The dmem address pin is driven every cycle, including nonmemory instructions, so keeping addresses in the shared `alu_result` register leaves that general path visible to timing. I’m separating the EX/MEM effective address into its own register and making the memory stage use that field; this keeps the address path isolated while retaining ALU results for forwarding and writeback."}}
