{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_59","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,180p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Iterative divider implementation\n\n## Changes\n\n- Replaced the ALU's combinational DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU operators with a\n  shared 32-step radix-2 restoring divider in `rtl/divider.sv`.\n- Added signed magnitude conversion and result sign correction. Divide by zero\n  returns the RV32M-defined all-ones quotient or original dividend remainder;\n  INT_MIN / -1 naturally returns INT_MIN with remainder zero.\n- EX starts the divider once, snapshots the forwarded operands for the eventual\n  RVFI payload, and holds the completed result until EX/MEM accepts it. While\n  running, EX/MEM receives bubbles and the hazard unit stalls IF and ID. The\n  existing data-memory stall can hold a completed result without reissuing the\n  operation.\n- Kept the `RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS` stand-ins combinational and disabled divider\n  stalls in that mode. Updated ALU cocotb tests to clock and check the iterative\n  result, and added the divider source to the pipeline test build.\n\n## Deviations and concerns\n\n- The divider lives under the ALU and uses explicit `start`, `busy`, `done`,\n  and `consume` signals. This keeps the ALU's M-operation selection together\n  while allowing EX to retain its normal single-cycle behavior for other ops.\n- Forwarding values can change while EX is stalled, so EX snapshots both\n  forwarded operands at divider start. This is needed both for RVFI source\n  operand reporting and to keep the final EX/MEM payload tied to the values\n  actually divided.\n- The divider adds 32 cycles to each nonzero DIV/REM instruction. CoreMark\n  cosim passes; the timing run reports 46.469 MHz and 2,558 logic cells for\n  placement option 0. No deep non-ALTOPS formal run was done locally.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint: pass.\n- `pytest -q cores/bench/test/test_*.py`: 5 passed.\n- Single-issue ALTOPS formal: 53 passed, 0 failed. The command used explicit\n  `CHECKS_CFG=formal/checks_si.cfg` and `WRAPPER=formal/wrapper_si.sv` because\n  this nested worktree path prevents `run_all.sh` from auto-detecting\n  `core.yaml`.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench NRET=1`: passed both ELF runs, including randomized\n  instruction and data stalls.\n- `make timing TARGET=bench`: placement option 0 reported 46.469 MHz.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
