 operators and route those operations through a shared iterative unit, preserving ALTOPS behavior and RV32M corner cases.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/divider.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a radix-2 iterative signed/unsigned divide-remainder unit with a ready/done interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Start and wait for divide operations, hold their EX/MEM payload until completion\n…[1256 of 4328 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:70e11d3ad25b7336]…\nt.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 106.08, \"delta_pct\": 775.25, \"vs_baseline\": 775.25, \"fmax_mhz\": 47.649, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491817, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2558, \"ff\": 630, \"seeds\": [46.469, 47.649, 47.649], \"perturbations\": [[0, 46.469, 23], [1, 47.649, 23], [2, 47.649, 23]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/id_ex_w.rs2_val_22_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -16.52, \"arrival_ns\": 26.814, \"logic_cells\": 47, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_hazard\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 23, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-30T05:10:52.491588Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-002-r1s1 (improvement, +775.25%): A 32-iteration EX divider pays when removing `/` and `%` materially shortens a divide-dominated critical path and CoreMark\\u2019s rare divides keep the stall cost below the Fmax gain.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
