{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -n 8 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20260930-002-r4s1\", \"title\": \"Split operand forwarding from execute\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The five-stage pipeline combines register-file operand selection and forwarding with the EX ALU and branch work in one timing region. Recent timing paths still traverse the register-file, ID, and EX logic, while the prior redirect-register experiment showed that retiming control alone pays an IPC penalty. A pipeline boundary after forwarded operand capture can shorten the data path without adding a cycle to ordinary instruction throughput.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The five-stage pipeline combines register-file operand selection and forwarding with the EX ALU and branch work in one timing region. Recent timing paths still traverse the register-file, ID, and EX logic, while the prior redirect-register experiment showed that retiming control alone pays an IPC penalty. A pipeline boundary after forwarded operand capture can shorten the data path without adding a cycle to ordinary instruction throughput.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Restructure the pipeline into separate operand and execute stages. Capture the fully forwarded source operands and instruction metadata in an operand stage, then perform ALU, branch resolution, and effective-address generation from those registered values in the following execute stage. Preserve one-instruction-per-cycle steady-state flow, but update forwarding and hazard control for the added stage, including load results, divider busy, memory backpressure, and redirect squashes. This should remove register-file and forwarding selection from the execute arithmetic path and raise Fmax; the added branch-resolution distance is the main IPC risk.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}