{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -n 8 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20260930-003-r2s2\", \"title\": \"Small dynamic branch target buffer\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark repeatedly executes conditional loop branches and direct control transfers, but the current core waits for EX resolution before redirecting fetch. The prior static predictor put instruction decode and target arithmetic on the fetch-to-PC path, damaging timing. A small learned target table can avoid that instruction-data dependency while predicting recurring branches after their first resolution.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark repeatedly executes conditional loop branches and direct control transfers, but the current core waits for EX resolution before redirecting fetch. The prior static predictor put instruction decode and target arithmetic on the fetch-to-PC path, damaging timing. A small learned target table can avoid that instruction-data dependency while predicting recurring branches after their first resolution.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add an eight-entry direct-mapped branch target buffer indexed by fetch PC bits [4:2], with a full upper-PC tag, target, and two-bit saturating direction counter per entry. Train it once when a valid branch or jump successfully resolves in EX, initializing a new conditional entry weakly toward its observed direction. On a tag hit, predict jumps taken and conditional branches according to their counter, selecting the saved target in IF; carry the predicted next PC through the pipeline and redirect only on a mismatch. This should remove recurring EX redirect bubbles without decoding imem_data or calculating an immediate target in the fetch address path. Gate table updates during stalls and suppress training for misaligned control transfers.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted-next-PC metadata to the fetch and ID/EX pipeline payloads.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Look up the current PC in a small tagged BTB and select its predic\n…[30462 of 33534 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:95cd884b5f58c391]…\n, \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 89.81, \"delta_pct\": -15.34, \"vs_baseline\": 641.01, \"fmax_mhz\": 40.341, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491817, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 8666, \"ff\": 649, \"seeds\": [40.067, 40.341, 40.341], \"perturbations\": [[0, 40.067, 26], [1, 40.341, 26], [2, 40.341, 26]], \"lutram\": 527, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs1_val_15_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -19.958, \"arrival_ns\": 30.252, \"logic_cells\": 56, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_rf\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 26, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-30T07:34:24.053997Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 5, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-001-r5s0 (regression, -15.34%): Per-bit one-hot masked-OR reads expanded each 31-row flop-based register-file port into a high-fanout decode and reduction network, whose area and routing cost outweighed removing the indexed-read bypass mux.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
