{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260930-002-r6s1/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md 2>/dev/null; rg -n \"16,384|16384|15750|15,750|DFFs|DFF|error|ERROR|Warning|warning\" cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260930-002-r6s1/cores/bench/generated/gowin_p0/impl/gwsynthesis/core_bench.log cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260930-002-r6s1/cores/bench/generated/gowin_p0/gw.log'","aggregated_output":"# Implementation notes\n\n- Added a four-entry in-order RAM store FIFO in MEM. An empty FIFO forwards an immediately accepted RAM store directly to dmem; a stalled request is captured and held stable at the FIFO head. New stores can be enqueued while an older store drains, including simultaneous pop/push when full.\n- Loads and non-RAM stores wait until older FIFO entries drain. Loads then wait for their own bus handshake; MMIO and other non-RAM stores remain synchronous. The MEM stall output now freezes the pipeline only for those cases or when a full FIFO cannot accept a store.\n- No decoder, RVFI format, or core top-level ports changed.\n- Formal: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed (`RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`).\n- Cosim: pass for selftest and CoreMark using `make cosim TARGET=bench NRET=1`. The unqualified command defaults to NRET=2 in this checkout and does not match bench's declared NRET=1.\n- Verilator lint: pass with the requested `-Wall` command.\n- Timing: `make timing TARGET=bench` failed during Gowin synthesis with `IF0008`: inferred `dmem_3` uses 16,384 DFFs, over the device limit of 15,750. No timing result was produced.\n- Concern: Gowin area/timing has not been validated because synthesis stopped at the dmem resource error. The RAM FIFO ordering and backpressure behavior passed the local formal and cosim gates.\ncores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260930-002-r6s1/cores/bench/generated/gowin_p0/gw.log:2:Fontconfig error: Cannot load default config file: No su