26-09-30 hyp-20260930-003-r3s2 (regression, -6.11%): A four-entry RAS can still regress CoreMark when canonical-return decode and EX-pop-adjusted stack-top selection feed IF's `next_pc`; even a small stack puts pre\n…[2847 of 5919 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:81cef6284231101c]…\n paths; carrying the token as a sideband to suppress validity and side effects preserves the datapath and improves fitness.\n- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-003-r11s2 (regression, -4.38%): Compressing a BTB entry to a 12-bit target does not remove prediction cost when `if_stage` still compares the full PC tag, decodes the fetched branch, checks its immediate, and selects the predicted PC; fetch-side logic can outweigh saved EX redirects for a single hot backedge.\n- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-001-r12s0 (regression, +1.80%): Direct `rs1`/`rs2` multiplier inputs remove `alu_src` from product generation, but the dependent-result path still passes through the ALU operation select and EX-to-ID forwarding, so bypassing an operand mux alone may leave the end-to-end limiter intact.\n- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-002-r12s1 (regression, -2.80%): Duplicating 32-bit ADD carry paths to move `alu_src` after the adder did not pay off in this core; the added adder area and routing outweighed removing operand selection from the carry chain.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
