{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-001-r8s0.yaml && git status --short'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260930-001-r8s0\ntitle: \"Share the RV32M multiplier datapath\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The ALU currently evaluates three separate 64-bit products for signed,\n  unsigned, and mixed-sign multiply operations. They share the same input\n  operands, while only one product is selected for a given instruction.\n  Reducing duplicated multiplier hardware can lower routing and placement\n  pressure in this small FPGA core.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the three parallel products with one 33-by-33 signed product.\n  Extend each operand with a sign bit selected by the multiply operation:\n  sign-extend both operands for MULH, only rs1 for MULHSU, and neither for\n  MULHU or MUL. The resulting product's low 32 bits serve MUL and its bits\n  [63:32] serve the high-half operations. This preserves RV32M bit results\n  while removing duplicate multiplier cones and reducing operand fanout,\n  which should ease placement and improve the timed datapath's Fmax.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Use one operation-configured 33-by-33 multiplier for MUL, MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU while preserving ALTOPS substitutions.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
