{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-002-r14s1.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260930-002-r14s1\ntitle: \"Resolve conditional branches in decode\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The five-stage core currently waits until EX to resolve conditional branches,\n  so each taken loop branch redirects fetch after younger sequential work has\n  entered the pipeline. CoreMark repeats these branches often enough that\n  reducing their recovery distance can improve iterations per cycle.\nhypothesis: |\n  Resolve conditional branches in ID using the source values already selected\n  by decode's forwarding network, and redirect fetch as soon as the branch is\n  accepted into ID/EX. Carry the resolved outcome and target with the branch so\n  EX records the correct retirement PC while suppressing a duplicate redirect.\n  Give older EX redirects priority, and qualify the early redirect with the\n  existing stall, valid, and squash conditions. This removes one stage of\n  taken-branch recovery without a predictor lookup on every fetch; the added\n  decode-to-PC compare and target path is the main timing risk.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Carry the early-resolved branch outcome and target through ID/EX.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare forwarded branch operands and compute the branch target while decoding.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Arbitrate the decode redirect against older EX redirects and existing stalls/squashes.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Apply accepted ID-stage branch redirects to the fetch PC.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Preserve resolved branch retirement metadata and avoid redirecting the branch again.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
