g gain outweighs CoreMark's added control-flow cycles. Preserve redirect behavior across imem and dmem stalls, prevent wrong-path side effects, and keep branch/jump RVFI pc_wdata and retirement precise.\nhyp-20260930-002-r3s1 | Use valid-only pipeline bubbles | regression delta 3.71 F 49.421 cycles 4491817 | cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0 -> dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s levels 14\n   Change ID/EX bubble insertion so flush only clears the stage valid bit while the payload registers continue capturing their ordinary inputs. Make EX suppress redirects and emit inert controls whenever its input is invalid, and qualify load-use detection with ID/EX valid so captured bubble payload cannot stall younger work. This removes the redirect-controlled clear mux from the wide ID/EX datapath and should shorten the reported register-file-to-ID feed\n…[7574 of 10646 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9e32f9b9abce7364]…\n-use behavior and bus-stall rules correct, and do not add a bubble for non-dependent instructions. The shorter EX-to-ID combinational path could improve Fmax, while the extra bubbles on immediate ALU dependencies may reduce CoreMark IPC; measure the tradeoff.\nhyp-20260930-002-r14s1 | Resolve conditional branches in decode | regression delta -28.05 F 47.715 cycles 4195392 | cpu/u_id/reg_q.imm_25_s0 -> cpu/u_if/pc_1_s0 levels 32\n   Resolve conditional branches in ID using the source values already selected by decode's forwarding network, and redirect fetch as soon as the branch is accepted into ID/EX. Carry the resolved outcome and target with the branch so EX records the correct retirement PC while suppressing a duplicate redirect. Give older EX redirects priority, and qualify the early redirect with the existing stall, valid, and squash conditions. This removes one stage of taken-branch recovery without a predictor lookup on every fetch; the added decode-to-PC compare and target path is the main timing risk.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
