{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_2", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 -c 'import json; p=\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\"; rows=[json.loads(x) for x in open(p)];\nfor x in rows:\n if x.get(\\\"category\\\")==\\\"structural\\\": print(\\\"\\\\n\\\",x[\\\"id\\\"],x.get(\\\"title\\\"),\\\"=>\\\",x.get(\\\"outcome\\\"),x.get(\\\"delta_pct\\\"),\\\"path\\\",x.get(\\\"critical_path\\\",{}).get(\\\"modules\\\")); print(x.get(\\\"hypothesis\\\",{}).get(\\\"hypothesis\\\", \\\"\\\")[:900] if isinstance(x.get(\\\"hypothesis\\\"),dict) else \\\"\\\")'\"", "aggregated_output": "\n hyp-20260930-002-r1s1 Iterative M-extension divider => improvement 775.25 path ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_hazard', 'cpu/u_id']\nReplace combinational DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU in the EX ALU with a shared radix-2 iterative divider. Hold the divide instruction in EX and stall younger pipeline stages until its quotient or remainder is ready, while allowing other instructions to retain their current single-cycle path. This removes the long divide network from the timed combinational path and should raise Fmax with little CoreMark cycle cost; preserve RV32M corner-case behavior and the formal ALTOPS substitutions.\n\n\n hyp-20260930-002-r2s1 Register branch redirect feedback => regression 4.29 path ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']\nAdd a registered branch/jump redirect boundary: capture the resolved\nredirect target and validity in EX, then apply the redirect and squash the\nyounger EX, ID, and fetch payloads on the following cycle. This breaks the\ncurrent same-cycle operand-to-hazard-to-ID feedback path and should raise\nFmax. It adds a recovery cycle for taken branches, so retain the change only\nif the timing gain outweighs CoreMark's added control-flow cycles. Preserve\nredirect behavior across imem and dmem stalls, prevent wrong-path side\neffects, and keep branch/jump RVFI pc_wdata and retirement precise.\n\n\n hyp-20260930-002-r3s1 Use valid-only pipeline bubbles => regression 3.71 path ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']\nChange ID/EX bubble insertion so flush only clears the stage valid bit\nwhile the payload registers continue capturing their ordinary inputs.\nMake EX suppress redirects and emit inert controls whenever its input is\ninvalid, and qualify load-use detection with ID/EX valid so captured\nbubble payload cannot stall younger work. This removes the\nredirect-controlled clear mux from the wide ID/EX datapath and should\nshorten the reported register-file-to-ID feedback path without adding\nbranch recovery cycles.\nPreserve load-use replay, bus-stall holds, divide interlocks, and the\nsingle-channel RVFI retirement contract.\n\n\n hyp-20260930-002-r4s1 Split operand forwarding from execute => broken None path None\nRestructure the pipeline into separate operand and execute stages. Capture the fully forwarded source operands and instruction metadata in an operand stage, then perform ALU, branch resolution, and effective-address generation from those registered values in the following execute stage. Preserve one-instruction-per-cycle steady-state flow, but update forwarding and hazard control for the added stage, including load results, divider busy, memory backpressure, and redirect squashes. This should remove register-file and forwarding selection from the execute arithmetic path and raise Fmax; the added branch-resolution distance is the main IPC risk.\n\n\n hyp-20260930-002-r5s1 Decouple fetch with a small instruction queue => regression 1.07 path ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']\nAdd a small FIFO between instruction fetch and decode, with each entry\ncarrying its instruction PC and word. Let fetch continue filling the FIFO\nwhile decode is held by downstream hazards or data-memory backpressure, and\nlet decode consume queued instructions when io_imemReady is low. This should\nhide some later instruction-bus stalls and improve CoreMark iterations per\ncycle without putting a predictor lookup on the fetch-address path. On an EX\nredirect, atomically discard younger queued entries and restart fetch at the\nredirect target; preserve response/PC alignment, bus-ready semantics, and\nprecise retirement through simultaneous stalls and redirects.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
