{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_1", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n -i '\\\"category\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\"structural\\\"|category: structural|pipeline|bypass|regfile|stage|fetch buffer|queue' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | tail -n 80\"", "aggregated_output": "2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260930-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Iterative divider to shorten the EX critical path\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline timing report shows a 199.8 ns path through forwarding and EX/ALU.\\nThe combinational divide and remainder operators are likely the deepest logic\\non this operand path and dominate the measured Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline timing report shows a 199.8 ns path through forwarding and EX/ALU.\\nThe combinational divide and remainder operators are likely the deepest logic\\non this operand path and dominate the measured Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU operators with a shared bounded\\niterative divider that captures operands and returns a quotient or remainder\\nafter 32 steps. Interlock the EX pipeline for those instructions only, keeping\\ntheir forwarding, retirement, divide-by-zero, and signed-overflow behavior\\nprecise. This removes the divider chain from the single-cycle EX timing path;\\nCoreMark should gain Fmax, with cycle cost only if its workload executes divides.\\nPreserve the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS stand-ins for formal runs.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 15, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Route DIV/REM operations through the shared iterative unit while retaining RV32M edge-case and ALTOPS behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/divider.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a bounded signed/unsigned iterative quotient-remainder datapath with captured operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Start and complete long-latency divide operation