{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category') == 'predictor':\n  print('\\\\n', d['id'], d['title'], d.get('outcome'), d.get('delta_pct'), d.get('critical_path',{}).get('arrival_ns'))\n  print(d.get('hypothesis',{}).get('hypothesis','').replace('\\\\n',' '))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\n hyp-20260930-003-r1s2 Static backward-taken fetch prediction regression 0.41 211.232\nPredict aligned backward conditional branches taken and direct JALs taken in IF, computing their targets from the fetched instruction. Carry the prediction bit through ID/EX and make EX redirect only on a direction mismatch or an unpredicted JALR. This should remove the EX redirect penalty on correctly predicted loop iterations while preserving recovery for forward branches and indirect jumps. \n\n hyp-20260930-003-r2s2 Small dynamic branch target buffer regression -5.19 28.508\nAdd an eight-entry direct-mapped branch target buffer indexed by fetch PC bits [4:2], with a full upper-PC tag, target, and two-bit saturating direction counter per entry. Train it once when a valid branch or jump successfully resolves in EX, initializing a new conditional entry weakly toward its observed direction. On a tag hit, predict jumps taken and conditional branches according to their counter, selecting the saved target in IF; carry the predicted next PC through the pipeline and redirect only on a mismatch. This should remove recurring EX redirect bubbles without decoding imem_data or calculating an immediate target in the fetch address path. Gate table updates during stalls and suppress training for misaligned control transfers. \n\n hyp-20260930-003-r3s2 Return address stack prediction regression -6.11 27.509\nAdd a four-entry return address stack that predicts only canonical JALR returns (rs1=x1, rd=x0, immediate=0), using the saved return PC as the speculative fetch target. Push PC+4 on resolved link-register calls and pop on resolved returns in EX. Carry the prediction and target with the instruction so EX suppresses redirect and pipeline flush only when the predicted target matches the resolved return target; retain normal redirect recovery on a miss or empty stack. The return classification and stack-top mux are simpler than a BTB tag lookup or branch-immediate adder, and should remove recurring return bubbles without adding arithmetic to the f\n…[4384 of 7456 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0a4b22b67dbbcc1b]…\nate mux path. On a prediction miss or any nonsequential fetch, leave prediction metadata invalid and retain the existing EX redirect recovery. Carry prediction metadata with each instruction and suppress redirects only when the resolved next PC matches its prediction, including not-taken recovery when a predicted-taken branch falls through. \n\n hyp-20260930-003-r10s2 Registered exact-tag hot backedge predictor regression -19.17 31.311\nAdd a single-entry, full-PC-tagged target predictor trained only by valid, aligned, taken backward conditional branches in EX. Register the prediction metadata as a sequential successor enters fetch, and use that metadata to select the saved target without putting the tag comparison on the PC update mux. Carry the prediction with the instruction and suppress EX recovery only when the resolved next PC matches; a tag miss or misprediction follows the existing recovery path. The small state captures a recurring hot loop while avoiding the alias recoveries of a short-tag predictor. \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
