{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-003-r13s2.yaml && git status --short'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260930-003-r13s2\ntitle: \"Exact-hit fetch decode bypass\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The prior one-entry backedge predictor reduced the target storage and\n  prediction metadata, but it still put fetched-instruction decoding and\n  immediate checks on the fetch address path. Those checks are redundant\n  after an exact fetch-PC tag hit because training only records resolved,\n  aligned conditional backedges.\nhypothesis: |\n  Keep a one-entry full-PC-tagged predictor for resolved taken conditional\n  backedges and store the target's low 12 bits. On an exact tag hit, use the\n  saved target directly without decoding imem_data or rebuilding the branch\n  immediate in IF; the entry itself certifies that this PC was a trainable\n  branch. Carry only the predicted-taken bit through ID/EX and let EX recover\n  on a not-taken outcome. This removes fetch-side decode and immediate\n  checking while preserving exact-PC matching and existing misprediction\n  recovery, reducing the logic on IF's PC-update path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Carry a one-bit predicted-taken marker through the fetch and ID/EX payloads.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use an exact full-PC tag hit to select the stored low-12-bit target without decoding the fetched instruction or checking its immediate.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Propagate the predicted-taken marker alongside the decoded instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Train only on valid aligned taken conditional backedges and redirect on direction mismatch.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect predictor training while preserving stall, redirect, and