ed target in IF; carry the predicted next PC through the pipeline and redirect only on a mismatch. This should remove recurring EX redirect bubbles without decoding imem_data or calculating an immediate target in the fetch address path. Gate table updates during stalls and supp\nLESSON: - 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-003-r2s2 (regression, -5.19%): A BTB removes `imem_data` from fetch prediction, but its indexed tag comparison and target mux still feed the IF PC update, so the lookup path can cost more timing than recurring EX redirects save.\n\n hyp-20260930-003-r3s2 Return address stack prediction regression fitness 99.6 delta -6.11\nHYP: Add a four-entry return address stack that predicts only canonical JALR returns (rs1=x\n…[8848 of 11920 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1db31efad4e1771c]…\narget mux on the PC update path or carrying a wide target through the pipeline.\nLESSON: \n\n hyp-20260930-003-r13s2 Exact-hit fetch decode bypass broken fitness None delta None\nHYP: Keep a one-entry full-PC-tagged predictor for resolved taken conditional backedges and store the target's low 12 bits. On an exact tag hit, use the saved target directly without decoding imem_data or rebuilding the branch immediate in IF; the entry itself certifies that this PC was a trainable branch. Carry only the predicted-taken bit through ID/EX and let EX recover on a not-taken outcome. This removes fetch-side decode and immediate checking while preserving exact-PC matching and existing misprediction recovery, reducing the logic on IF's PC-update path.\nLESSON: - 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-003-r13s2 (broken, n/a): An exact-PC IF prediction can still break `rvfi_pc_fwd` if speculative PC advance and EX mismatch recovery do not agree on the next retired PC, so validate squash-token and retirement-PC alignment for predicted branches.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
