{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-003-r14s2.yaml')\ns=Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')\nprint(p.resolve())\nprint(p.read_text())\nprint('schema:', s.exists())\nif s.exists():\n print(s.read_text())\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-luna_xhigh-v2-rep3/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260930-003-r14s2-hypgen/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-003-r14s2.yaml\nid: hyp-20260930-003-r14s2\ntitle: \"Verify one-entry backedge predictions at resolution\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Taken loop branches repeatedly redirect fetch after EX resolves them. Earlier exact-PC backedge predictors kept lookup small but failed to preserve precise next-PC recovery for arbitrary instruction streams, and broader predictors reduced Fmax. A single trained entry can capture a hot loop while keeping the fetch-side logic and state limited.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a one-entry predictor trained only by valid, aligned, taken conditional backedges whose target stays in the branch PC's 4 KiB page. Match the full fetch PC and store the target's low 12 bits; on a hit, speculatively fetch that target without decoding imem_data. Carry the hit and predicted target checkpoint with the instruction. In EX, compare the resolved architectural next PC against that checkpoint for every instruction, including non-branches, and redirect to the resolved next PC on any mismatch. This handles changing instruction contents, changed branch immediates, and not-taken outcomes; the existing squash token must kill the fetched wrong-path instruction before it can retire or cause side effects. The small target checkpoint costs some pipeline state, but removes the earlier predictor's unverified-hit failure mode while avoiding full-width target metadata.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Carry predictor-hit state and a 12-bit predicted-target checkpoint from fetch to EX.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a one-entry full-PC-tagged same-page backedge predictor and select its saved target on exact hits.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Capture the predictor checkpoint with the corresponding instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare the checkpoint with the resolved next PC and request recovery for every prediction mismatch, including non-branches.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire predictor training and mismatch redirects through existing stall and squash-token control.\"\n\nschema: True\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"id\",\"title\",\"category\",\"motivation\",\"hypothesis\",\"expected_impact\",\"changes\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\":       {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\"},\n    \"title\":    {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
