{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-003-r2s2.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260930-003-r2s2\ntitle: \"Small dynamic branch target buffer\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  CoreMark repeatedly executes conditional loop branches and direct control transfers, but the current core waits for EX resolution before redirecting fetch. The prior static predictor put instruction decode and target arithmetic on the fetch-to-PC path, damaging timing. A small learned target table can avoid that instruction-data dependency while predicting recurring branches after their first resolution.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a small direct-mapped branch target buffer indexed by the registered fetch PC, with a tag, target, and two-bit saturating direction counter per entry. Train it once when a valid branch or jump successfully resolves in EX. On a tag hit, predict jumps taken and conditional branches according to their counter, selecting the saved target in IF; carry the predicted next PC through the pipeline and redirect only on a mismatch. This should remove recurring EX redirect bubbles without decoding imem_data or calculating an immediate target in the fetch address path. Gate table updates during stalls and suppress training for misaligned control transfers.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Add predicted-next-PC metadata to the fetch and ID/EX pipeline payloads.\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: Look up the current PC in a small tagged BTB and select its predicted target without using imem_data.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Carry fetch prediction metadata from IF/ID into ID/EX.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Detect prediction mismatches and provide one-shot resolved control-flow training data.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Connect EX resolution feedback to the IF predictor and preserve existing stall and redirect recovery behavior.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
