branches, but prior predictors\n  lowered fitness because instruction decode, tag comparison, or return-stack\n  selection became part of the fetch PC update path. The eight-entry BTB\n  regression specifically showed a long lookup and feedback path, while the\n  unpredicted pipeline pays recurring EX redirect bubbles.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a compact four-entry tagged BTB with a two-bit conditional direction\n  counter, trained from resolved branches and jumps in EX. Stage the lookup\n  for the sequential successor PC one fetch ahead and register its hit,\n  direction, and target alongside the PC, so the current fetch selects a\n  registered prediction rather than doing a table tag compare and target\n  mux in the PC update cycle. Invalidate that staged result on a redirect\n  or predicted-taken transfer, then resume sequential lookahead; retain EX\n  mismatch recovery and suppress BTB updates for invalid or misaligned\n  control transfers. This should preserve recurring loop predictions while\n  moving predictor lookup off the critical redirect-to-PC feedback path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Carry the staged BTB hit, direction, and target metadata with fetched instructions.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Implement a four-entry tagged BTB and register sequential-successor lookup results separately from the PC update.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Propagate staged prediction metadata into ID/EX for resolution comparison.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare actual control flow with the staged prediction and provide resolved BTB training events.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire predictor training and preserve stall, redirect, and recovery alignment.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
