{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-003-r9s2.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260930-003-r9s2\ntitle: \"Sequential lookahead branch target prediction\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Repeated CoreMark branches and direct jumps currently redirect only after EX resolution, but earlier predictors reduced Fmax by putting instruction decode, a target-table lookup, or stack selection on the fetch PC update path. A small exact-tag predictor can still remove recurring redirect bubbles if its lookup is prepared as the sequential successor PC enters fetch.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a four-entry direct-mapped BTB for conditional branches and direct JALs, using full PC tags, saved targets, and two-bit direction counters for conditional branches. While fetching PC, look up PC+4 and register that prediction metadata only when the next PC advances sequentially; use the registered metadata for the current instruction's predicted next PC. This moves the BTB read and tag comparison off the PC update mux path. On a prediction miss or any nonsequential fetch, leave prediction metadata invalid and retain the existing EX redirect recovery. Carry prediction metadata with each instruction and suppress redirects only when the resolved next PC matches its prediction, including not-taken recovery when a predicted-taken branch falls through.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add prediction-valid, predicted-taken, and predicted-target metadata to the fetch and ID/EX bundles.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a four-entry full-tag BTB and register lookahead prediction metadata for the sequential successor, invalidating it on nonsequential PC changes.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Carry fetch prediction metadata into ID/EX with its instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Generate training data for resolved conditional branches and direct JALs, and redirect only when actual next PC differs from the carried prediction.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect EX predictor training to IF while preserving existing stall, redirect, and squash-token behavior.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
